Workstream ID: calm-interface
Title: Make normal CareerOS pages calmer and action-first
Status: DONE
Milestone: Deliver a calmer action-first interface with authorized publication evidence
Dependencies: tracker-foundation, tutorial-and-help, omscs-path-explorer
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/14
Purpose: Reduce default interface prose across the portal. Keep actions and
  meaningful data prominent, put secondary explanations in concise accessible
  contextual help, reserve useful procedural teaching for the optional tutorial
  and delete redundant copy. Do not treat learning content or user records as
  disposable interface clutter.

Tasks:
  [x] Audit routed surfaces and capture representative before states.
  [x] Classify essential data/warnings, contextual help, teaching and deletion.
  [x] Reuse or add one small accessible click/hover/keyboard help pattern.
  [x] Make OMSCS choices and its companion action-first.
  [x] Put Discovery Atlas above Tracking and group Georgia Tech under Education.
  [x] Reverify OMSCS-only course choices and remove campus-only UI references.
  [x] Distinguish source-backed hard prerequisites from recommended preparation.
  [x] Apply deliberate copy/hierarchy decisions across the other normal pages.
  [x] Move useful procedures into appropriate isolated tutorial/help lessons.
  [x] Preserve actual data, controls, confirmations, errors and study content.
  [x] Qualify desktop/mobile, both themes, help interactions and affected flows.
  [x] Update focused documentation, evidence and this issue/Project mapping.
  [x] Restore consistent group spacing above Tracking after owner visual feedback.

Acceptance criteria:
  The normal OMSCS paths page exposes its next-term action, real draft budget
    and useful choices without introductory essays or repeated reassurance.
  All normal routed surfaces have an explicit audited disposition. Static
    guidance is edited intentionally, not hidden by global paragraph/opacity/
    font-size rules. User-authored records and intentional reading content remain.
  Sidebar order is Discovery Atlas, Tracking, Education and Career. Georgia
    Tech remains on its stable route under Education; all counts and records
    retain their meaning. Desktop and compact navigation stay usable.
  Useful context is available by click/tap, keyboard and hover, with accessible
    naming, Escape/outside dismissal, sensible focus return and viewport bounds.
    No important explanation is hover-only.
  Required consent, irreversible-action warnings, stale/conflicting saves,
    validation errors and material academic/credit conflicts stay visible where
    the decision is made. Compact help never silently changes business rules.
  New enrollment choices, presets and recommendations are supported by the
    current official OMSCS catalogue. In-person-only references are not course
    choices. Online catalogue membership does not promise a particular term.
  Source-backed hard prerequisites/grade/permission conditions are visible
    and respected by proposed ordering. Recommended background is separate;
    do not invent enforced registration rules from soft preparation advice.
  The tutorial may grow, but only useful teaching moves there. Existing step
    identities/order, real-control action gates and practice isolation survive.
    Redundant motivational/policy repetition may be deleted outright.
  Do not shrink the established type scale, replace source learning workbooks,
    rewrite frozen editions or change actual progress/storage/journal semantics.
  Existing user previews stay running. Qualification uses disposable contexts,
    never a real owner profile or private record manipulation.
  Keep local verification, human review and publication separate. Source
    publication requires a separate explicit owner decision and exact hosted
    evidence; the November 21 release is tracked by current-site-publication.

